## Original Content
Hillel Wayne explains why formal methods like TLA+ matter, how they help build reliable software, and whether AI will finally bring formal verification into the mainstream.

## Summary
Hillel Wayne explains the importance of formal methods like TLA+ in developing reliable software. He also explores how AI could bring formal verification into the mainstream of software engineering.

## Key Points
- Formal methods, such as TLA+, are essential for building reliable and error-free software systems.
- Formal verification helps prevent software bugs and enhances system stability by providing mathematical proofs.
- AI has the potential to make formal verification more accessible and widely adopted in the software industry.
- Understanding and applying formal methods can lead to more robust and secure software development practices.


